no-OS licensing
===============

no-OS is, by default, licensed under the permissive BSD-3-Clause license.
The full text of that default license is in the LICENSE_BSD file.

The authoritative license for any individual file is the one declared in
that file's own header: an SPDX-License-Identifier tag or, for some
third-party and vendor code, a full license header. Some files and whole
directory trees are under other terms -- other permissive licenses or
proprietary vendor device-API licenses.

For the complete picture -- how licenses are declared, the LICENSES/
directory of full license texts, and the repository-local LicenseRef-
identifiers used for proprietary vendor device-API code -- see:

    doc/sphinx/source/license_rules.rst


A note on aggregation
---------------------

The mere aggregation of these files (putting them side by side in one
source repository) does not create a single master license for all of
them. When you build a project that combines files, it is up to you to
ensure the individual licenses are compatible. Some proprietary ADI
vendor-API trees forbid combination with incompatible code outright, and
you may not distribute a binary that violates the terms of any file it
includes.

Nothing in this file restricts, limits, or supersedes the license terms of
any particular file.
